  <prompt>BLOCKED until UAC-r2 answers Q1-Q4 in `notes/coordination/2026-10-08-to-uac-r2-model1-guests.md` (owner 2026-10-08: this project makes the change, after UAC-r2's input, to keep their rules). Under provisioning D2, Model 1 customer users are B2B guests in Spaarke's tenant (`tid` = Spaarke, `acct = 1`, `idp` = home tenant). G1: `scripts/Set-ExternalFlagForB2BGuests.ps1` (required by the deployment guide) flags every `#EXT#` systemuser `sprk_isexternal = true`. G2: `WorkforceIdentityOptions.cs:6-9` / D-13 assume Model 1 staff sign in with the customer's `tid`, so `WorkforceMembershipTest.Evaluate` denies them. G3: guest contact binding never binds by email.</prompt>
  <goal>On a Model 1 stamp, guests whose home tenant is the customer's are treated as internal staff by the external flag, the workforce member test and contact binding; every other guest stays external/denied; the D-13 comment and the deployment guide match D2. Exact rules per UAC-r2's answers.</goal>
  <constraints>
    <constraint>Do not start until the owner relays UAC-r2's answers; implement exactly the agreed rule; spec/ADR conflicts → escalate (CLAUDE.md 6.5).</constraint>
    <constraint>Do not edit UAC-r2's `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/*` or `SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion*`; add new tests elsewhere unless UAC-r2 agrees.</constraint>
    <constraint>BFF §10 obligations (placement, publish size, CVE, tests); dev BFF deploy and any `-Apply` of the script only with the owner's go.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit tests: a customer-home-tenant guest is internal / a member / binds by email; a guest from any other tenant is external / denied / strict; Model 2 behaviour unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The script's dry run lists only non-customer guests on a Model 1 stamp; the guide and the D-13 comment describe D2.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <justification>
